t compact font glyph only under the producer blank-mask guard. Writes HUD_X and target framebuffer glyph cells; preserves stage/lives and existing MMU ownership. Clobbers A/B and follows the existing render interface. Source: src/main.s and src/shared_text_runtime.inc. Current capacity and integration qualification are recorded in <a href="../tickets/bug-061-global-two-digit-part-format.html#split-formatter-fit-20261003">BUG061</a>.</p></section><section id="routine-highscore-helper-stage-player-score"><h3><code>stage_player_score</code></h3><p>BUG-069 approved prototype; not integrated production. Existing mapped stage helper paints six score digits at x33–38,row2 in light green during hidden hydration. Context2 reads current SCORE_BCD; contexts0/1 paint zero. Existing stage_panel_char preserves loop registers; score accounting and MMU ownership remain unchanged.</p></section><section id="routine-resident-runtime-life-marker-position"><h3><code>life_marker_position</code></h3><p>BUG-062 capacity prototype for the approved 12-slot reserve grid. Input A is the slot index 0–11; the routine returns the authored tile root through HUD_X/HUD_Y and does not access lives, player state or reserve count. It is called from draw_lives with JSR after relocation to the immutable shared text region. All twelve coordinate pairs were compared with the approved grid formula. This is assembly/layout evidence only; it is not runtime acceptance.</p><p>Source: src/main.s and src/shared_text_runtime.inc. The helper’s source contract and capacity qualification remain preparation evidence.</p></section></main>
